              "summary": "**Analyzing analyst confidence**\n\nI'm looking into whether analyst confidence depends on their forecasts and all the report answers. I want to aggregate responses like A=3 and B=2. It seems that confidence could be based on personal signals and peer recommendation accuracy. Also, I wonder if each peer recommendation counts as one vote with a reliability of .6. But there’s a caution that confidence shouldn’t be a guarantee. Lastly, I find the total of surveys and peers' signals crucial to consider.**Decoding survey signals**\n\nI think the analysts may base their posterior assessments on survey signals and possibly shared information. I could interpret the report confidence as a probability of forecast accuracy while treating the responses as categorical observations with reliability. However, I’m not sure if I should count each observation as distinct. They seem to imply that every observation only counts once, possibly due to overlapping peer reports, even though the initial surveys were distinct. This feels a bit tricky!",
